{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-start-species-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.71. `scale-county-start-species`: a county inventory over `scale-county-timeagg-year`'s county database (`inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg.esm`), NOT aggregated -- July 2020, the weekday, hour 7, road types 1 and 4, output Hour -- for the gasoline passenger car (21) and the diesel combination long-haul truck (62), selecting START EXHAUST only: THC, CH4, N2O, the six ATRatio air toxics (benzene, ethanol, 1,3-butadiene, formaldehyde, acetaldehyde, acrolein), NMHC, NMOG, TOG, VOC, Atmospheric CO2, Total Energy, CO2 Equivalent, and the PM species (PM10, PM2.5, OC, EC, sulfate, non-EC PM, aerosol water). MOVESOutput is 3,521 rows.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is the start-exhaust species no earlier capture selected (PLAN.md §7.3.69 found them silent): N2O, whose only rate is at opModeID 100, the mode StartOperatingModeDistributionGenerator weights at 1 for polProcessID 602 after the start mode distribution (StartOperatingModeDistributionGenerator.java:434-458) -- the model weighted it 0, so start N2O was 0 and CO2 Equivalent short by it; the six toxics' ATRatio, which FuelEffectsGenerator evaluates from generalFuelRatioExpression's START strings for model years 2001 and later (a property factor times a ratio of exponentials whose exponents carry RVP and second-order standardized terms the running strings do not) and from the Complex Model's start configurations (2002, 2402, 2502, 2602 over VOC 8702) for 2000 and earlier; and the start PM species.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "hotelling-adjustment",
      "time-aggregation",
      "starts",
      "output-time-step"
    ]
  },
